WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.436
-Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.337
I'm Jimmy Fallon,
anchoring hour 30

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:09.609
of NBC's election-night
coverage.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.143
Come on. It's 2020.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.212
Did you really think last night
would end up wrapped up

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.481
with a neat little bow?

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.416
Seriously, today, it felt like
waking up with a hangover,

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.852
then realizing
you're still at the bar.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.421
"What time is it?"

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:24.290
What a long, emotional, and
confusing ride this has been.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.361
It's like a Matthew McConaughey
car commercial that won't end.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.062
Meanwhile, you think
you're stressed.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.630
Imagine how
President Trump feels.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.899
In two months,
he's either getting

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.502
inaugurated or incarcerated.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.503
It was a crazy night.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:38.638
Here's what most people heard

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.106
right before they went to bed.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.273 line:0%
-Too close to call.

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:43.008 line:0%
-Too close to call.
-Too close to call.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.210 line:0%
-Too close to call.
-Too close to call.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.949
-Yeah, the one thing we know for
sure is, no more polls.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.652
That's it. Done, okay?
No more polls, alright?

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.687
From now on, the only time
Americans want to hear

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.989
about a poll is if
they're talking about Santa

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.491
or strippers.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.426
♪♪

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.662
Yep, today, pollsters saw
a different blue wave

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:06.666
right as they were slowly
walking into the ocean.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.735
At this point,
I'd rather hear predictions from

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.871
the guy trying to guess my
weight at a carnival.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.273
Pollsters were basically us
when we really think

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.409
we've nailed a parallel park but
then get out of the car

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.444
and see we're about
14 feet from the curb.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.979
It's like, "Honey, look out.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.614
You don't want to scrape
the bottom of the do--

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.350
Oh, actually, well,
we could fit a Le Car

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.119
between where we parked
and where the..."

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.754
-Le Car.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:31.491
I knew you'd laugh at "Le Car."

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.225
From now on,
when you release a poll,

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:34.727
just say both candidates
are tied

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.863
with a margin of error of 100.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:41.401
As we speak, some states are
still tallying the votes.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.536
Somehow, Chuck E. Cheese
can count a million tickets

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:47.440
on the spot, and we still can't
count the votes in three days?

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.007
I can't take
the suspense anymore.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:51.344
My stress eating has gone from
brownies to ice cream

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:54.914
to just pouring raw cake mix
down my throat.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.249
Yep, the race is
still too close to call.

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:59.085
Apparently,
a lot of voters looked at

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.354
90,000 COVID cases a day
and thought,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.089
"Sure, I can do
four more years of this."

00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:06.892
Experts still can't believe
the race is this tight.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:09.428
Apparently, people were voting
based on which candidate

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:13.165
they want to drink bleach with.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.934
But one of the big stars of
the election night

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.235
was America's sweetheart

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:19.539
and MSNBC political
correspondent Steve Kornacki,

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.940
who is on our show this evening.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.375
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.744
Guy was working the touch-screen
map like a magician.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.514
All night long, he was shown on
the "Kornacki Cam."

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:29.616
You see that?

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.183
MSNBC basically treated him like

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.821
a panda that was about to
give birth.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.488
Last night was incredibly tense,

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:38.524
and you could tell
the newscasters were feeling it.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.793
Even CNN's graphics guy,
who does the banner

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.361
at the bottom of the screen,
was stressed out.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.862
Take a look at this.

00:02:43.862 --> 00:02:47.166 line:0%
-And when Florida's close, it
comes down to the I-4 corridor.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.135 line:0%
-But a tremendous amount of
Democratic vote

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.669 line:0%
are still outstanding at...

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:53.640 line:0%
-You know, that's nearly
30 points there -- 28 points.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.508 line:0%
-That puts him at
17,000, 18,000 votes.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.545 line:0%
-With this
wild and different 2020,

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.947 line:0%
mail-in voting,
in-person early voting.

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:04.717 line:0%
If he saw this and,
say, it's past midnight...

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.985 line:0%
The question is,

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.586 line:0%
is that just the early votes
or are there votes?

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:08.721 line:0%
Wayne County...

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.223 line:0%
-And they are going to
count ballots

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.558 line:0%
that come in postmarked
by Election Day.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.894 line:0%
-It was no longer off the map,

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.562 line:0%
like they thought it was
after 2016.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:17.763 line:0%
-And, so, what I'm
trying to do is

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.399 line:0%
identify where, specifically,
in this county...

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.668
-He's moving to Belgium.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.803
He's moving to Belgium.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:27.873
Well, very early this morning,
Biden spoke to a drive-in crowd

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:32.311
in Wilmington, Delaware, and he
told us that we need patience.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.914
But I'm not sure it's
one of America's strengths.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.550
I mean, if a TikTok video isn't
fun in the first 3 seconds,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.052
we're like, "Ah, next."

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.689
Yeah, we just have to be
patient in a country

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.157
that literally invented
a Domino's tracker

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.359
so we know exactly
when our pizza will arrive.

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:51.964
Like, "It's in the oven, honey!
It's in the oven!

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.967
He's almost here!
He's almost here!

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:59.372
Honey, wave to him.
Make sure he knows it's us."

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.540
But this is very interesting.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.408
Joe Biden actually
got more votes

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:05.011
than any other candidate
in history.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.112
-Wow.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:09.481
-Yeah.

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:14.587
So, once again,
how is this even close?

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.689
Meanwhile, Trump spoke
from The White House

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.424
early this morning,
and he seemed upset

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.827
that the results weren't
immediately called in his favor.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.027
Watch this.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.797
-We were getting ready
for a big celebration.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.932
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.133
-We were winning everything.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.769
And, all of a sudden,
it was just called off.

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:34.440
Literally, we were just all
set to get outside

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.911
and just celebrate something
that was so beautiful, so good.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.446
-Aww. That's too bad.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:44.383
I'd hate for the election to get
in the way of a good party.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.819
Yeah, Trump also lashed out at
the voting process

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.087
and made a pretty bold claim.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.188
Take a look at this.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:52.959
-This is a fraud
on the American public.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.461
This is an embarrassment
to our country.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.530
We were getting ready to win
this election.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.266
Frankly, we did win
this election.

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:04.337
-Yeah. If you're keeping track,
in the same speech,

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:07.072
Trump claimed the election was
a fraud and an embarrassment

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.908
and then declared victory.

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:11.577
I don't think
we should correct Trump.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.612
Just nod along,
put him in a fake White House,

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:14.613
and let him spend
the next four years

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:15.748
thinking he's in charge.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:18.350
Who cares, right?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.786
Well, as you can might expect,
Trump has been

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:22.055
tweeting a lot today, and you
could tell he's getting worried,

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.356
because one of his posts said...

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.864
Dude, they're not finding votes.

00:05:32.864 --> 00:05:35.635
They're counting them.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:38.471
Because no one wanted to
leave the house

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.507
because there's a pandemic!

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.842
Gosh!

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.210
Trump's getting close to
being like,

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.244
"Okay, forget about the votes.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:48.948
Let's measure
this thing in retweets."

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.349
Oh, and before
we go any further,

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.985
here's some extremely important
election news.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.520 line:0%
-Voters in New Jersey
have passed

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.821 line:0%
a constitutional amendment

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.957 line:0%
legalizing
recreational marijuana.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:04.997
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:08.968
-That's right --
weed is legal in New Jersey.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.869
You just know there's
already guy walking around

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:12.237
in a tie-dye track suit.

00:06:12.237 --> 00:06:14.239
He's like, "Excuse me.

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:17.343
You guys like, uh...

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.677
You guys like Phish?

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.679
You like the Phish?

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:21.914
Like the Phish.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:24.717
May wake up with a fish
in your bed. A fish."

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:27.019
♪♪

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.455
Listen, when you're home to
the Jets and Giants,

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:32.191
you got to make drugs legal.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.126
Now that weed is legal,
New Yorkers

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:35.828
driving into New Jersey
are gonna go from

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.663
rolling their windows up
to rolling them down.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.965
It's like, "Ahh!"

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.400
And this makes sense.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.969
Once Jersey legalized weed,
they also voted to put a Wawa

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:47.139
on their state flag.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.041
So far, legalized weed
has been a little rough.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:53.179
Every time the mob buries
a snitch, they forget where.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:55.547
But if you think legal weed
is a big deal,

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:57.650
just listen to what Oregon did.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.453 line:0%
-Oregon voters passing measure
to decriminalize

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:03.656 line:0%
small amounts of cocaine,
heroin, and other drugs.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.124
-I'm sorry.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:12.364
I'm sorry.
A small amount of heroin?

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:14.200
Who is only doing
a small amount --

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.700
Show of hands --
does anyone know someone

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.703
who casually does heroin?

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:18.837
Just a little bit?

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:20.506
"I just do it on the weekends.

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:21.974
Yeah, I do it sometimes
when I drink."

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:25.611
I do heroin -- a little bit."

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.145
And, finally, earlier today,

00:07:27.145 --> 00:07:29.915
Gap tried to send
a message of unity over Twitter

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:32.451
by posting a short video of a
red-and-blue hoodie

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:33.619
with the caption...

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:38.958
Kind of weird, right?

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.292
Trying to bring
the country together

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:43.396
when your name is The Gap.

